{
 "uid": "rl-cache-live",
 "title": "RL cache decision engine - live replay",
 "tags": [
  "rl-cache"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
 "schemaVersion": 39,
 "version": 1,
 "editable": true,
 "refresh": "2s",
 "time": {
  "from": "now-5m",
  "to": "now"
 },
 "templating": {
  "list": [
   {
    "name": "policy",
    "label": "policy",
    "type": "query",
    "datasource": {
     "type": "prometheus",
     "uid": "prom"
    },
    "query": {
     "query": "label_values(rlcache_action_total, policy)",
     "refId": "p"
    },
    "refresh": 2,
    "includeAll": false,
    "multi": false,
    "current": {
     "text": "agent (RL model)",
     "value": "agent (RL model)"
    },
    "sort": 1
   }
  ]
 },
 "annotations": {
  "list": []
 },
 "panels": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "How to read this",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 3
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**What you see:** the trained reinforcement-learning model and four simple rules replay the SAME stream of cache requests in the simulator, side by side, in fast-forward. Every cache miss makes the policy choose one of 45 actions (how long to keep the item, how protected it is, where to store it). Lines higher on *hit ratio* and *utility* and lower on *stale reads* are better. *Utility U* = hits + 0.5 x speed score - 3 x stale cost (the project's selection score). Data may be SYNTHETIC or a real Twitter sample (see the info panel). Pick a policy in the **policy** drop-down to see its action mix."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Hit ratio now (model)",
   "description": "Reads served from the cache in the last ~10 s.",
